        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lyons_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The land encompassing Lyons was originally inhabited by the Potawatomi people before European-American settlement began in the late 1830s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lyons_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lyons is home to Wag-Aero, a company that specializes in manufacturing aircraft parts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lyons%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The White River flows through Lyons, providing local opportunities for canoeing, kayaking, and fishing.",
